@startuml Discovery & Registration Flow
title Discovery and Registration Stage - Component Architecture
skin rose
skinparam shadowing true

package "User / CLI" {
  [pts discovery\\ndiscover] as cli_discover
  [pts seeds\\nseattle] as cli_seeds
}

package "Discovery Engine" {
  [CatalogClient] as catalog_client
  [Verifier] as verifier
  [Scorer] as scorer
}

package "Output" {
  [Discovery Dossier\\n(dossier.json)] as dossier
}

package "Registration Engine" {
  [pts discovery\\nregister] as cli_register
}

package "PostgreSQL" {
  [(jurisdictions)] as jurisdictions_db
  [(probes)] as probes_db
}

' Entry points
cli_discover --> catalog_client : searches catalog.data.gov
catalog_client --> scorer : returns candidates
scorer --> verifier : scores top 5
verifier --> scorer : probes platforms
scorer --> dossier : writes dossier with\\nscores and maps
dossier --> cli_register : input for register
cli_register --> jurisdictions_db : stores jurisdiction config
cli_register --> probes_db : stores probe results
cli_seeds --> jurisdictions_db : seeds default config\\n(seattle-kingcounty-wa)

note right of dossier
  Dossier contains:
  - Candidate rankings
  - Platform probes
  - Field map guesses
  - Status map guesses
  - Validation notes
end note

legend right
  <b>Components:</b>
  
  <b>CatalogClient</b>: Searches catalog.data.gov via CKAN API
  - Queries for jurisdiction permit datasets
  - Returns ranked candidates
  
  <b>Verifier</b>: Probes platform endpoints
  - Detects platform type (Socrata/CKAN/Other)
  - Validates API accessibility
  
  <b>Scorer</b>: Ranks candidates with weighted factors
  - Platform compatibility
  - Dataset freshness
  - Record count
  - Field coverage
  
  <b>Jurisdictions Table</b>: Central registry
  - Identity (slug, name)
  - Source (dataset_id, platform)
  - Config (field_map, status_map)
  - Active/inactive flag
  
  <b>Probes Table</b>: Platform test results
  - Endpoint validation
  - Feature detection
  - Error logs
  
  <b>Data Flow:</b>
  1. Discovery searches catalog → scores candidates → writes dossier
  2. Registration reads dossier → stores to jurisdictions + probes
  3. Seeds directly loads pre-configured jurisdictions
endlegend

@enduml